From: Alsey Coleman Miller <alseycmiller@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] build: let a cross build produce the typelib

build_gir is switched off for every cross build, whatever -Dintrospection
says:

  build_gir = get_option('introspection') and g_ir_scanner.found() and not
              meson.is_cross_build()

so configure reports "Introspection : NO" while still accepting
-Dintrospection=true, and no GWeather-4.0.typelib is produced. Anything that
reaches libgweather through introspection then fails at runtime rather than
at build time - gnome-shell aborts on

  JS ERROR: Error: Requiring GWeather, version 4.0: Typelib file for
    namespace 'GWeather', version '4.0' not found

The assumption behind the guard is that g-ir-scanner cannot run against a
cross build, which is not true of every build system: a scanner wrapper that
knows how to run target binaries handles it, and the other twenty-one
typelibs gnome-shell asks for are built that way in the same tree.

Leave the decision to -Dintrospection and to whether g-ir-scanner is
actually there.

Upstream: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libgweather/-/issues
Signed-off-by: Alsey Coleman Miller <alseycmiller@gmail.com>

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -51,7 +51,7 @@
 gen_locations_variant = find_program('build-aux/meson/gen_locations_variant.py')
 
 g_ir_scanner = find_program('g-ir-scanner', required: get_option('introspection'))
-build_gir = get_option('introspection') and g_ir_scanner.found() and not meson.is_cross_build()
+build_gir = get_option('introspection') and g_ir_scanner.found()
 build_docs = get_option('gtk_doc') and build_gir
 
 schemas_srcdir = meson.project_source_root() / 'schemas'
